==== Flash Layout ====
Please check out the article [[docs:techref:flash.layout]]. It contains an example and a couple of explanations.

==== OEM easy installation ====

This section deals with how you install OpenWrt from a device freshly opened.  Plus the steps required such as reset to factory defaults if the device has already been configured

**Note:** Reset router to factory defaults if it has been previously configured.
  * Browse to ''%%http://192.168.1.1/adv_index.htm%%''
  * Select Administration, then Firmware Upgrade from menu to left of screen.
  * Select browse and locate the openwrt-15.05-ar71xx-nand-r6100-ubi-factory.img file
  * Select the Upload button
  * The firmware file will be validated and the current firmware version and the uploaded version will be displayed.
  * Select the Yes button to transfer the firmware file to the router.
  * Wait for upload to finish and router to reboot
  * Telnet to 192.168.1.1 and set a root password, or browse to ''%%http://192.168.1.1%%'' if LuCI is installed.

==== OEM installation using the TFTP method ====

->  [[docs:guide-user:installation:generic.flashing.tftp]]

The bootloader contains a "firmware recovery" mode where it acts as a TFTP server.  Firmware recovery mode can be entered by holding down the reset button while turning the power on.  The power LED will first light steady orange, then flashing orange, and finally flashing green.  At that point the bootloader is ready for firmware recovery and you can release the reset button.  (Firmware recovery can also be initiated by typing "fw_recovery" at the bootloader serial console.)

In firmware recovery, the router's IP address is 192.168.1.1.  Connect to one of the LAN ports and set your PC to a static address in the 192.168.1.X range.  Use a TFTP client to PUT an .img file to the router, either stock firmware or a "factory" OpenWrt binary.  Be sure the TFTP client is using "binary" mode.  Once the file has transferred, the router will flash it and reboot automatically.

For a how-to on Windows, have a look at [[https://kb.netgear.com/22688/How-to-upload-firmware-to-a-NETGEAR-router-using-TFTP|How to upload firmware to a NETGEAR router using TFTP]].

==== Upgrading OpenWrt ====
->  [[docs:guide-user:installation:generic.sysupgrade]]

If you have already installed OpenWrt and like to reflash for e.g. upgrading to a new OpenWrt version you can upgrade using the mtd command line tool. It is important that you put the firmware image into the ramdisk (/tmp) before you start flashing.

=== LuCI Web Upgrade Process ===

  * Browse to ''%%http://192.168.1.1/cgi-bin/luci/mini/system/upgrade/%%'' LuCI Upgrade URL
  * Upload image file for sysupgrade to LuCI
  * Wait for reboot

=== Terminal Upgrade Process ===

  * Login as root via SSH on 192.168.1.1
  * Use the following commands to upgrade.

<code>
cd /tmp/
wget https://downloads.openwrt.org/chaos_calmer/15.05/ar71xx/nand/openwrt-15.05-ar71xx-nand-r6100-squashfs-sysupgrade.tar
sysupgrade /tmp/openwrt-15.05-ar71xx-nand-r6100-squashfs-sysupgrade.tar
</code>


