==== Opening the case ====
**Note:** This will void your warranty!

Remove the three obvious screws in the bottom.  Separate the front cover from the rest of the case by releasing two clips on each side and three across the top.  The board faces away from the front cover, to access the serial port etc. remove the board from the back half of the case being careful not to stress the antenna cables.

//Main PCB//

**Photo of PCB**

==== Serial ====
-> [[docs:techref:hardware:port.serial]] general information about the serial port, serial port cable, etc.

The serial port is a 4 pin header on the board above the WAN port and next to the smaller shield box that contains the 5 GHz radio.  Pins on the port are from top (closest to the antennas) to bottom (closest to the Ethernet ports): +3.3V, TX(from router), RX(to router), Ground.  The bootloader uses a baud rate of 115200 N81.

